|passage=A loose nocking point is equally dangerous since it may result in what is known as a {{'}}'''dry''' release' when the arrow merely falls from a string a few feet away as the bow is shot. This may distort or weaken the bow.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1992|title=Pennsylvania Game News|volume=63|page=57
|passage={{...|Anyone who can pull through a 100-pound bow with such a letoff can hold full draw at 35 pounds. [...]}} most like "'''dry''' firing," or a '''dry''' release, wherein the string meets no resistance.}}
